FINAL ANSWER:
**Short answer:** Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson hold most of the code that survives at HEAD. Together they hold about 70% of the lines. Troy's figure depends on one identity guess.

**Surviving lines at HEAD, default `git blame -w -M -C`, non-blank lines (1,664 attributed):**

| Author | Lines | Share | Commits | Commit share | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode (2 addresses, merged, guess) | 649 | 39.0% | 95 | 30.1% | 2026-04-10 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 551 | 33.1% | 143 | 45.3% | 2021-09-07 |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 80 | 4.8% | 2 | 0.6% | 2024-05-14 |
| Jon Church | 59 | 3.5% | 3 | 0.9% | 2026-01-16 |
| Sebastian Beltran | 57 | 3.4% | 2 | 0.6% | 2025-07-23 |
| Ulises Gascón | 46 | 2.8% | 3 | 0.9% | 2026-01-22 |
| Ignacio Mangas | 38 | 2.3% | 2 | 0.6% | 2025-12-01 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 30 | 1.8% | 5 | 1.6% | 2015-05-28 |
| Linus Unnebäck | 26 | 1.6% | 1 | 0.3% | 2016-11-07 |
| Ollie Buck | 14 | 0.8% | 1 | 0.3% | 2019-06-05 |

The other 52 authors hold 6.9% together. The largest of them is Eric di Domenico at 0.7%.

**Troy Goode, unmerged:** `<email redacted>` holds 605 lines (36.4%, 93 commits). `troy@laptop.example` holds 44 lines (2.6%, 2 commits). The tool suggests they are one person because the name matches. That is a guess from names and addresses. Only you can confirm it. Without the merge, Troy is still first, at 36.4%.

**Alejandro Caravaca Puchades:** `<email redacted>` appears under two names, so the tool counts it as one person here (30 lines, 1.8%). The proposed `.mailmap` line is `Alejandro Caravaca Puchades <<email redacted>> alex94puchades <<email redacted>>`. That is also a guess until you confirm it.

**Bus factor:**
- Merged: 2 authors reach 50% (Troy and Douglas, 72.1%). 4 authors reach 80%.
- Unmerged: 2 authors reach 50% (Troy and Douglas, 69.5%). 5 authors reach 80%.
- Scope is the whole repository, counted in non-blank lines.

**What was left out:**
- `dependabot[bot]`: 10 lines and 11 commits excluded.
- Reformat: `.git-blame-ignore-revs` ignores one commit. I did not confirm its sha. The likely candidate is 62628c0, "style: reformat js with 4-space indent".
- Mechanical rewrites: the tool did not set any commits aside. It flagged five commits that look mechanical and kept them in the numbers:
  - 739dc11 (Douglas, license reformat, 17 lines)
  - fcd2b56 (Troy, ESLint switch, 14 lines)
  - 00d6eec (Douglas, 9 lines)
  - 344ce1e (Douglas, 1 line)
  - 9c2b59d (Douglas, 1 line)
  I did not inspect them with `git show --stat`. Together they hold 42 lines. Even if all 42 were moved off Douglas, the top two would not change.

**Not shown by this tool:** the quality of the lines, review, design documents, and code deleted on purpose. Line share measures what survived, not merit.

I did not write a `.mailmap`, because you asked a question and did not ask for one. Say so if you want the suggested lines written as a proposal, or if you want the five mechanical commits checked with `--ignore-rev`.

